approach:
The vulnerability lies in the `vuln()` function:
```c
void vuln() {
    char buf[32];
    fgets(buf, 128, stdin);  // BUG: reads 128 bytes into 32-byte buffer
    printf("You entered:, %s\n", buf);
}
```

The developer attempted to secure the program with `fgets()` but made a critical mistake: passing `128` as the size instead of `sizeof(buf)` (32). This allows writing 128 bytes into a 32-byte buffer, triggering a stack overflow.
